      "math_academy_id": "q-319197",
      "problem": "Calculate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $4$ | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |",
